stery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0998efd9-3539-4d38-b793-9a6d9c23ce4f","uuid":"f0bf045c-7910-4d7b-a98f-d66f23d22fad","timestamp":"2026-10-15T13:11:07.919Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"challenges/day15/scripting-crumb-trail/solver/powerplay.py:75:    \"\"\"JSON descriptor from the base64 literal; tolerate a reversing/XOR $reconstruct block in variants.\"\"\"\nchallenges/day15/scripting-crumb-trail/solver/solve.py:240:        out[\"property\"] = \"mixed\" if dot and brk else \"bracket_literal\" if brk else \"dot\"\nchallenges/day15/scripting-crumb-trail/solver